{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it","id":965959,"title":"Awws what a lovely Human, lets keep it","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-08T18:17:14-07:00","id":965959,"title":"Awws what a lovely Human, lets keep it","content":"Im very fascinated about how garou society and kinfolks work. im still gathering info on WtA and learning more and more.<br /> my questions here are involving the following issues<br /> can a normal human (average joe) become a kinfolk? how is the process? can a Children be adopted by garous and be turned into a kinfolk?<br /> <br /> and what would garou's think about adopting a human?, situation: werewolves fight fomoris, civs in the cross fire. the battle ends and they find a little girl shouting for her mommy as one of the fomori's -agonizing- is noming on her mother's body, allowing her a few moments of life to say goodbye to her daughter before dying. the garous kill the beast and save the girl, now she is traumatized and she seen them in Crinos form (delirium as usual) but they know that pentex has its claws everywhere and they cant leave her at an orphanage or let it become an &quot;stadistic in the system.&quot; nor they coudnt find any relatives of the girl who could take care of her<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T18:29:03-07:00","id":965966,"title":"","content":"Not unless you're using rites from the CoG Revised tribebook, but that also includes a rite that involves having sex in Crinos and another that's encouraged to be something that can insta-cleanse BSDs of taint, so it is... suspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T18:38:51-07:00","id":965972,"title":"","content":"No to there first paragraph. Being kinfolk is hereditary, and breeds out over a few generations.<br /> <br /> For the second part, I'm sure it has to have happened over the course of history. The best thing that can be done (to take care of her) for example-girl is to be adopted out to a kinfolk family. Garou make terrible parents. The Curse is only part of it, and that won't every really be overcome. She would be better off with a normal human family though. But if that isn't an option and the Garou want her taken care of for whatever reason, kinfolk are the way to go. If she stays within the community, her children will likely end up kinfolk and she will be contributing to Garou society that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T19:41:00-07:00","id":965993,"title":"","content":"what about long exposure to Crinos? would that eventually help her &quot;Not to go into Delirium&quot; ? or thats impossible","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T19:56:06-07:00","id":966003,"title":"","content":"Well, that would be buying up Willpower to 7+. If the human does not go insane, I imagine that repeated exposure to Crinos would justify increasing Willpower, though it is probably easier just to select a human who is already strong-willed (around 14% have Willpower 7+ if I remember correctly). I would say, however, that I would be open to the idea of a human woman who bears a Garou/Kinfolk child becoming Kinfolk during her pregnancy, because of the Gaian forces flowing through her during her pregnancy, though there is nothing in canon to suggest such a transformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T21:33:12-07:00","id":966035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=965993#post965993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what about long exposure to Crinos? would that eventually help her &quot;Not to go into Delirium&quot; ? or thats impossible</div> </div> </div> </div>That could justify her buying up Occult, so that she could roll Wits + Occult to move up on her effective Willpower rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T22:15:38-07:00","id":966055,"title":"","content":"Either way, I think repeatedly exposing a little girl to Delirium's effect would probably cause a lot more issues than it would solve. And while Garou are far from humane, that is straight psychological torture.<br /> The chances of getting a contributing member of society out of that aren't great. Better to remove the girl from being directly involved with Garou if you are taking the angle of caring for her well being.<br /> Alternatively there is a higher rank (Homid?) Gift that immunizes someone to Delirium, though I don't remember for how long. You can probably go on a quest for some sort of spirit intervention to help prolong it if you really felt it necessary. But all this strikes me as a bit overboard fort the initial premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T04:35:27-07:00","id":966148,"title":"","content":"Hm, what about the idea of a woman who bears Kinfolk/Garou children being transformed into Kinfolk by the Gaian energies flowing through her during her pregnancy? While there is nothing to support that rule in canon, I doubt that it would majorly effect the game, though it would make it marginally easy to adopt a woman into the Kinfolk (just knock her up).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T06:37:26-07:00","id":966177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=965972#post965972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No to there first paragraph. Being kinfolk is hereditary, and breeds out over a few generations.<br /> <br /> For the second part, I'm sure it has to have happened over the course of history. The best thing that can be done (to take care of her) for example-girl is to be adopted out to a kinfolk family. Garou make terrible parents. The Curse is only part of it, and that won't every really be overcome. She would be better off with a normal human family though. But if that isn't an option and the Garou want her taken care of for whatever reason, kinfolk are the way to go. If she stays within the community, her children will likely end up kinfolk and she will be contributing to Garou society that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this happens like one session out of three in a Werewolf LARP. Leaving orphans alone to the predations of the Wyrm is easily read as violating several tents of the Litany.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T15:22:26-07:00","id":966462,"title":"","content":"One of the hardest things for Werewolf players to deal with are the mortal family members of fomori and/or the Kinfolk of Black Spiral Dancers. I generally think that the Kinfolk of the Children of Gaia in Canada and the USA take care of those unfortunates and allow them to interbreed if they are not Tainted. Of course, there is a question of what happens when COG Kinfolk breed with BSD Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:25:43-07:00","id":967393,"title":"","content":"the Kinfolk unsung heroes book says that some people have BECOME kinfolk, through interaction with garou society, its not a common occurence but is noteworthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:25:12-07:00","id":967424,"title":"","content":"I had forgotten about that. How long do you think it would take to become one of the Kinfolk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:54:07-07:00","id":967442,"title":"","content":"Id like to see a system in the W20 kinfolk book.<br /> <br /> another thing? Id like for the Garou to have a rite to at the very least , ensure reincarnation for worthy humans, amongst kin bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T00:29:41-07:00","id":969066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=967393#post967393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Kinfolk unsung heroes book says that some people have BECOME kinfolk, through interaction with garou society, its not a common occurence but is noteworthy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a page reference ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There is the &quot;Rending the Veil&quot; Punishment Rite that doesn't necessarily end the Delirium, but any human so punished will not forget (and possibly go crazy). That the sheer idea of finding a human scumbag, performing the Rite and reveal the fact that werewolves exist to terrorize him kind of goes against the Litany is one of the aspects of the game, never really explained.<br /> <br /> The Children of Gaia Rite, that is the friendlier version of the Punishment Rite is not only in the revised TB, but was in the 1st Edition TB, too. In addition to the no delirium, the target really becomes kinfolk, adding one vital characteristic. According to the Curse rules, kinfolk is less affected by the curse than humans. This is the whole reason they can work together and have long relationships.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:51:03-07:00","id":969398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=969066#post969066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have a page reference ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There is the &quot;Rending the Veil&quot; Punishment Rite that doesn't necessarily end the Delirium, but any human so punished will not forget (and possibly go crazy). That the sheer idea of finding a human scumbag, performing the Rite and reveal the fact that werewolves exist to terrorize him kind of goes against the Litany is one of the aspects of the game, never really explained.<br /> <br /> The Children of Gaia Rite, that is the friendlier version of the Punishment Rite is not only in the revised TB, but was in the 1st Edition TB, too. In addition to the no delirium, the target really becomes kinfolk, adding one vital characteristic. According to the Curse rules, kinfolk is less affected by the curse than humans. This is the whole reason they can work together and have long relationships.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Page 28 Kinfolk Unsung heroes Professor Warners commentary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T14:41:53-07:00","id":969462,"title":"","content":"Although it doesn't specifically<i> say it</i>, I sort of automatically assumed that Prof Warner's statement was actually talking about the Rite of the Parted Veil. The Rite is a closely guarded secret among the CoGs (as it <i>technically</i> violates the Litany), and I would think that they would talk about that sort of thing in a guarded way around outsiders. The rules as stated are pretty clear that what Warner actually says in that passage is a flat impossibility...<br /> <br /> <i>Although</i>... there <i>is</i> the Unknowing Kinfolk merit in Project Twilight, that looks exactly like what Warner is talking about. IE: They aren't <i>exactly</i> humans in the first place, but &quot;lost&quot; Kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 09-14-2016, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T15:53:18-07:00","id":969505,"title":"","content":"it seemed odd to me on that Merit that they remained Somewhat susceptable to the Delerium until they learned of and accepted their place in garou society.<br /> <br /> Especialy as in MANY other cases it mentions kinfolk being identified by the fact they dont Cower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-14-2016, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T00:45:13-07:00","id":969730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=969398#post969398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 28 Kinfolk Unsung heroes Professor Warners commentary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, well, since this is in direct reference to the Children of Gaia I, like Uniform Two Six, always assumed that &quot;I can substantiate the fact that certain humans have become Kinfolk with nurturing and acculturation.&quot; meant, that a human was vetted for and eventually subjected to the Rite the tribe has.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=969505#post969505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it seemed odd to me on that Merit that they remained Somewhat susceptable to the Delerium until they learned of and accepted their place in garou society.<br /> Especialy as in MANY other cases it mentions kinfolk being identified by the fact they dont Cower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as often with White Wolf, it makes a difference if you see the word from a werewolf chronicle point of view, or a Project Twilight Chronicle point of view. In the latter it is certainly a merit, even if you have to &quot;grow into it&quot;. In a chronicle where the PCs are garou, it is more of a flaw, if you aren't recognisable as kin at first glance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T06:37:05-07:00","id":969859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=969505#post969505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it seemed odd to me on that Merit that they remained Somewhat susceptable to the Delerium until they learned of and accepted their place in garou society.<br /> <br /> Especialy as in MANY other cases it mentions kinfolk being identified by the fact they dont Cower.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A Crinos Garou should incite PST the first time you see it, even if you're immune to the Delirium. Kinfolk learn to trust that the Ragemonster is under control, unless of course it isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:15:21-07:00","id":969920,"title":"","content":"oh on the SAD? How difficult would it be for a kinfolk in the SAD to steer them away from the Garou or get them chasing fake leads.<br /> <br /> oh the Long Whispers, or Dire Call Talens how worthwhile are they for such a infiltrator<br /> <br /> one problem is if the SAD FINDS such people it will probaly be more driven then ever to curtail the supernatural<br /> <br /> especialy if they find a previous DIRECTOR OF THE DIVISION, was intentionaly steering it on behalf of his supernatural masters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-15-2016, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:45:45-07:00","id":970345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=969920#post969920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh on the SAD? How difficult would it be for a kinfolk in the SAD to steer them away from the Garou or get them chasing fake leads.<br /> <br /> oh the Long Whispers, or Dire Call Talens how worthwhile are they for such a infiltrator<br /> <br /> one problem is if the SAD FINDS such people it will probaly be more driven then ever to curtail the supernatural<br /> <br /> especialy if they find a previous DIRECTOR OF THE DIVISION, was intentionaly steering it on behalf of his supernatural masters.</div> </div> </div> </div> That whole point is emblematic of the Garou as a whole. You want to keep the Veil intact and stop the humans (particularly a government that possesses <i>nuclear weapons</i>) from learning of your existence? Just murder a few FBI agents and leave their <i>dismembered corpses</i> lying around. Brilliant idea.<br /> <br /> Once said FBI agents are a pile of chunky salsa and the FBI is now twigging to the concept that werewolves are a thing, just murder the director and maneuver one of your Kin into the position (since<i> that </i>will hold forever).<br /> <br /> Once the government gets impatient with the <i>total lack of progress </i>your plant has achieved and sack him for his 'incompetence' (which you're lucky if that's <i>all</i> they figure is going on), you then put another of your Kin in the agency (who also happens to be <i>his daughter </i>-- because <i>that's</i> not tempting fate), to try to interfere with them learning about werewolves... Y'know, even though that cat has been out of the bag since <i>friggin' 1973</i>!<br /> <br /> <br /> The description of the Garou in Project Twilight is spot-on. They are reactionary and have almost no ability to be proactive or use strategy, and are entirely focused on playing catch-up and doing rearguard actions. Now admittedly, House Wyrmfoe was (at the time) under a clearly insane king (Jacob Morningkill), but assassinating the DSAD was one of the most monumentally idiotic things the Garou have done in the 20th century, and their approach to the FBI since then has not markedly improved. To put it another way, if the government thinks that werewolves are this disorganized rabble, their approach is going to be entirely different than if they find that they've been quietly knocking off government officials and trying (and to a degree <i>succeeding</i>) to subordinate the national security infrastructure. The only way that works is if they actually think that they can maintain that dynamic forever. The moment that that fails, the werewolves are in a world of hurt.<br /> <br /> And the Silver Fangs are the ones who should be more cognizant of that than any other tribe. Clan Crescent Moon <i>still</i> hasn't recovered from 1917!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:05:58-07:00","id":970392,"title":"","content":"Garou really need to keep their cool when they face FBI agents or else problems will occur. The main problem with the FBI is that their agents are likely to remember a Garou in Crinos because they have above average Willpower. Of course, the rarity of Werewolves make it statistically unlikely that an FBI agent will ever encounter one (a 1:500,000 chance is very long odds), but there are nearly 14,000 FBI agents, and a few of them are going to stumble on Garou every year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 09-15-2016, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:18:19-07:00","id":970442,"title":"","content":"I was wondering if Marsha Crowe or Martin Fiske were found out, would it be safe to say the true believers would be offended to see themselves being used as pawns.<br /> <br /> and finding GENERATIONAL infiltrators, would probaly really raise some hackles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:38:47-07:00","id":970450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=970345#post970345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That whole point is emblematic of the Garou as a whole. You want to keep the Veil intact and stop the humans (particularly a government that possesses <i>nuclear weapons</i>) from learning of your existence? Just murder a few FBI agents and leave their <i>dismembered corpses</i> lying around. Brilliant idea.<br /> <br /> Once said FBI agents are a pile of chunky salsa and the FBI is now twigging to the concept that werewolves are a thing, just murder the director and maneuver one of your Kin into the position (since<i> that </i>will hold forever).<br /> <br /> Once the government gets impatient with the <i>total lack of progress </i>your plant has achieved and sack him for his 'incompetence' (which you're lucky if that's <i>all</i> they figure is going on), you then put another of your Kin in the agency (who also happens to be <i>his daughter </i>-- because <i>that's</i> not tempting fate), to try to interfere with them learning about werewolves... Y'know, even though that cat has been out of the bag since <i>friggin' 1973</i>!<br /> <br /> <br /> The description of the Garou in Project Twilight is spot-on. They are reactionary and have almost no ability to be proactive or use strategy, and are entirely focused on playing catch-up and doing rearguard actions. Now admittedly, House Wyrmfoe was (at the time) under a clearly insane king (Jacob Morningkill), but assassinating the DSAD was one of the most monumentally idiotic things the Garou have done in the 20th century, and their approach to the FBI since then has not markedly improved. To put it another way, if the government thinks that werewolves are this disorganized rabble, their approach is going to be entirely different than if they find that they've been quietly knocking off government officials and trying (and to a degree <i>succeeding</i>) to subordinate the national security infrastructure. The only way that works is if they actually think that they can maintain that dynamic forever. The moment that that fails, the werewolves are in a world of hurt.<br /> <br /> And the Silver Fangs are the ones who should be more cognizant of that than any other tribe. Clan Crescent Moon <i>still</i> hasn't recovered from 1917!</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of that has to do with presentation of the Garou across editions. Prior editions beat the fish out of water and outdatedness drums hard. W20 has them starting to catch up fairly effectively, while also noting that many problems are more dug in and hidden than they might have been shown to be in an earlier edition.<br /> <br /> Also, given how much trouble various intelligence agencies had with rival sects of vampires and other things shaking up their rolls in Hunter's Hunted 2, I don't think that the modern Garou have much to worry about unless they really, really, really screw up, because the only ones who do unofficial SAD stuff are only a few steps above Bob Schnoblin in terms of agency support and respectability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:04:35-07:00","id":970464,"title":"","content":"And those who do Official SAD Stuff?<br /> <br /> But your right, the X20 version of SAD Isnt even worth infiltrating anymore, hopefully why Marsha Disappeared to settle down marry and start bearing Garou offspring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T22:13:51-07:00","id":970488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=970464#post970464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue a