:1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-16-2016, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T11:32:12-07:00","id":988313,"title":"","content":"Yes. I do not think that skindancers would even be capable of entering Erebus to seek purification, so they would be considered to be cowards by any definition used by the Garou. They are incapable of withstanding purification, they would have to use poison, stealth, etc to kill a Garou, etc. Since they require five Garou skins for their Rite, they are selfish because they are sacrificing five warriors for Gaia for their ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T11:38:56-07:00","id":988317,"title":"","content":"if one DID try using this rite to create a skindancer academy, Id have his conspiracy faily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T12:05:06-07:00","id":988965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=988317#post988317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if one DID try using this rite to create a skindancer academy, Id have his conspiracy faily.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would allow it, hell I'd push for it. Would make for a damn interesting campaign and meta change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T12:42:47-07:00","id":988982,"title":"","content":"I really, really doubt that the Garou would tolerate the existence of a skindancer academy. I imagine that they would hunt down and annihilate everyone who was associated with the organization and, quite likely, no one could hide from them. It would likely end up in the news as a cult mass murder, where the people dressed up as wolves and killed each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T14:47:46-07:00","id":989028,"title":"","content":"So, i havent been able to get the Kinfolk20 book (Damn you chilean credit cards!!), can someone give me the cliff notes to see if its possible or how to turn a human into kinfolk?<br /> <br /> also, just wondering..do mages can be considered as Kinfolks? i mean, can they reproduce with garous or they need a special capacity in order to breed garous/kinfolks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T15:08:09-07:00","id":989034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=989028#post989028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, i havent been able to get the Kinfolk20 book (Damn you chilean credit cards!!), can someone give me the cliff notes to see if its possible or how to turn a human into kinfolk?<br /> <br /> also, just wondering..do mages can be considered as Kinfolks? i mean, can they reproduce with garous or they need a special capacity in order to breed garous/kinfolks?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b&quot;<b>Rite of the Parted Veil</b>. Level five. This rite is the Children of Gaia's ultimate gift to Gaia-cherishing humans. When performed, the Veil is not pierced (as in the deadly Rite of Rending the Veil) but parts seamlessly to admit one or more humans (or wolves!). The person on whom the rite is performed thus becomes Kinfolk. Two Children unrelated to the human must witness that he loves Gaia and would aid the Children's cause. Most often this rite is done for mates of Garou or Kin. Some of the Patient Deed say that they hope to extend the rite to whole nations. The rite consists of the Garou dancing round the subject, while the ritemaster chants from the Songs of Welcome. A the rite progresses, the Garou slowly shapeshift, until they assume the Crinos form without frightening the human.<br /> <b>System:</b> The ritemaster makes an extended Wits + Rituals roll, difficulty of the human's Willpower. He must accumulate successes equal to the human's age before the rite succeeds; children are easier to &quot;adopt&quot; than adults.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 10-17-2016, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T15:48:32-07:00","id":989048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=989034#post989034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b&quot;<b>Rite of the Parted Veil</b>. Level five. This rite is the Children of Gaia's ultimate gift to Gaia-cherishing humans. When performed, the Veil is not pierced (as in the deadly Rite of Rending the Veil) but parts seamlessly to admit one or more humans (or wolves!). The person on whom the rite is performed thus becomes Kinfolk. Two Children unrelated to the human must witness that he loves Gaia and would aid the Children's cause. Most often this rite is done for mates of Garou or Kin. Some of the Patient Deed say that they hope to extend the rite to whole nations. The rite consists of the Garou dancing round the subject, while the ritemaster chants from the Songs of Welcome. A the rite progresses, the Garou slowly shapeshift, until they assume the Crinos form without frightening the human.<br /> <b>System:</b> The ritemaster makes an extended Wits + Rituals roll, difficulty of the human's Willpower. He must accumulate successes equal to the human's age before the rite succeeds; children are easier to &quot;adopt&quot; than adults.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In the name of the players of my troupe.. I OWE YOU A BEER!<br /> <br /> Also, thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T16:16:06-07:00","id":989062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=988982#post988982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really, really doubt that the Garou would tolerate the existence of a skindancer academy. I imagine that they would hunt down and annihilate everyone who was associated with the organization and, quite likely, no one could hide from them. It would likely end up in the news as a cult mass murder, where the people dressed up as wolves and killed each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see a Red Talon Using curse of Lycaon on a few of the &quot;Students&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;so you want to be wolves, then you can be wolves!&quot; <br /> <br /> is a fiting and appropiate end. to such scum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T17:44:02-07:00","id":989090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=988965#post988965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would allow it, hell I'd push for it. Would make for a damn interesting campaign and meta change.</div> </div> </div> </div>whys it interesting if I could ask?<br /> <br /> See what kind of losers they could attract or what.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T18:49:39-07:00","id":989123,"title":"","content":"Instead of the typical wyrm storyline you have an up and coming tribe of essentially traitors (good or bad depends on how you wanna run the skin dancer sas) which would lead to different enemies. Instead of shock troops and wyrm spawn you've got werewolves who got used to killing werewolves while they were human. I'd argue there's a much more interesting danger factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:04:10-07:00","id":989133,"title":"","content":"if you want good ideas why it just wouldnt work, I can think of a few..<br /> <br /> One is that the spirits empowering the rite will have NOTHING to do with skindancers.<br /> <br /> Another is that skindancers are generally cowardly and self destructive.<br /> <br /> another point, part of what distinguishes skindancers is their generally solitary nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:26:05-07:00","id":989143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=989133#post989133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you want good ideas why it just wouldnt work, I can think of a few..<br /> <br /> One is that the spirits empowering the rite will have NOTHING to do with skindancers.<br /> <br /> Another is that skindancers are generally cowardly and self destructive.<br /> <br /> another point, part of what distinguishes skindancers is their generally solitary nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think only 1 of those 3 points is valid, and that's the first one (which I agree 100% with).<br /> <br /> I've no idea why it's been said (a few times now) that Skindancers are cowardly. I'd agree they are more than a bit corrupt, but you are talking about people so fed up with the way things are done that they are killing off Gaia's warriors, sometimes even before becoming Garou themselves.<br /> <br /> And the third point, is just completely wrong. Seeing as how you have to have someone teach you the Rite, which includes years of tutelage, they really can't be all that solitary. And if you alter that (to make more sense) where the Rite can be performed for a kinfolk, then they really end up clustered up. Offhand, the first2 places that come to mind to me for skindancers are the W20 adventure, where there is a pack and the one or 2 Caerns they have (in Pariahs). Both books imply that they are social creatures. If they weren't they probably wouldn't have lasted as long as they have now. Hell, the most solitary one is probably Haight himself, and even he took apprentices obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:26:17-07:00","id":989144,"title":"","content":"You must not forget that skindancers are among the most selfish entities in the WoD. They have to kill five werewolves to become skindancers and, quite frankly, I cannot think that they would be anything but bad guys because they are irrevocably tainted by the Wyrm due to the nature of the rite. In addition to their selfishness and their association with the Wyrm, they deprived Gaia of five of her warriors, so they have done more damage to Gaia than the vast majority of the servants of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> One thing to consider though, what was the motivation of the Garou Kinfolk who helped to hunt down the Native American Garou and the Australian Garou? Were they just assisting their Garou kin or were they manipulating their Garou kin in order to gain the skins of the slain Garou? I imagine that the skindancers actually predate Samuel Haight and, during times of turmoil, the Wyrm has allowed disaffected Garou Kinfolk to learn the Ritual of Sacred Rebirth in order to turn Garou Kinfolk against the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:29:09-07:00","id":989146,"title":"","content":"I remember hearing in an earlier book that Sam haight &quot;Rediscovered&quot; the rite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:38:31-07:00","id":989153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=989146#post989146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember hearing in an earlier book that Sam haight &quot;Rediscovered&quot; the rite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> Also, you don't actually have to hunt down Garou to use it either. You can use the pelts of Garou who've fallen in battle or even died of natural causes.<br /> There is no reason that a previous version of the Rite had to be Wyrm tainted.<br /> <br /> Technically speaking, since a Garou should be able to survive skinning (if careful), there may not even be an actual need to have a dead Garou for the Rite at all. Admittedly, I think that line of thought is a bit more far fetched but it is worth noting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:44:09-07:00","id":989157,"title":"","content":"Albrecht survived it.<br /> <br /> Hmmmn makes me wonder was it created by the wyrm deliberately, to weaken the garou nation, or possible due to some cosmic fluke<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:55:04-07:00","id":989161,"title":"","content":"It may have been a perfectly Gaian rite to recycle her warriors, and it was corrupted by the Wyrm to put an end to that. Just think of how much stronger the Garou nation would be if they had a non corrupted Rite of Rebirth. They could elevate any promising kinfolk they wanted if you skin the Garou alive. And even if they have to be dead, you could still potentially get back 1 warrior for every 5 fallen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T20:02:22-07:00","id":989166,"title":"","content":"had thought of a Rank 5 Gift, that mimics, legends about &quot;Infecting&quot; people with lycanthropcy, it would be game breaking in a number of ways, but seems compelling given what it says in hammer and klaive<br /> <br /> &quot;Gaia NEEDS champions willing to challenge the gods&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> oh just thought, somethingi I've wondered for a while, does a would be skindancer fall under the nagahs purview, or do they have to wait until hes finished gathering skins and completed the rite<br /> <br /> I think its a valid question.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-17-2016, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T20:30:13-07:00","id":989175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=989166#post989166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">had thought of a Rank 5 Gift, that mimics, legends about &quot;Infecting&quot; people with lycanthropcy, it would be game breaking in a number of ways, but seems compelling given what it says in hammer and klaive<br /> <br /> &quot;Gaia NEEDS champions willing to challenge the gods&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> oh just thought, somethingi I've wondered for a while, does a would be skindancer fall under the nagahs purview, or do they have to wait until hes finished gathering skins and completed the rite<br /> <br /> I think its a valid question.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It depends on the Skindancer involved if the Nagah interfere or not.<br /> Example: John Little is a devoted kinfolk of the Shadow Lords, while helping his Sept he discovers a cache of material including the Rite of Sacred Rebirth. He realizes he can do this and begins to collect the 5 skins by following along behind the Sept when they attack a Black Spiral Dancer Hive. He gathers the necessary skins. The Nagah more than likely will ignore him.<br /> <br /> Example: John Broody is a Fianna Kinfolk forced to marry a Garou who treats him like shitte. He finds the Rite of Sacred Rebirth and embraces the Skindancer way. He starts with his wife/forced lover/baby Mamma and skins her after poisoning her. He then tries for an Elder of the local Sept,, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T21:14:59-07:00","id":989179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=989175#post989175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It depends on the Skindancer involved if the Nagah interfere or not.<br /> Example: John Little is a devoted kinfolk of the Shadow Lords, while helping his Sept he discovers a cache of material including the Rite of Sacred Rebirth. He realizes he can do this and begins to collect the 5 skins by following along behind the Sept when they attack a Black Spiral Dancer Hive. He gathers the necessary skins. The Nagah more than likely will ignore him.<br /> <br /> Example: John Broody is a <b>Fianna </b>Kinfolk forced to marry a Garou who treats him like shitte. He finds the Rite of Sacred Rebirth and embraces the Skindancer way. He starts with his wife/forced lover/baby Mamma and skins her <b>after poisoning her</b>. He then tries for an Elder of the local Sept,, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I may see a flaw in this disaffected kin's cunning plan...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T21:17:10-07:00","id":989180,"title":"","content":"LOL, just a quick example. But I thought of the flaw as I typed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T21:22:30-07:00","id":989183,"title":"","content":"on my other thread I asked a question, think that &quot;The curse of Lycaon&quot; is a suitably ironic punishment, for a would be skindancer?<br /> <br /> &quot;You want to become a wolf?&quot; Allright!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T23:22:13-07:00","id":989233,"title":"","content":"You could poison Garou with silver dust in their food and drink. A milligram a day would probably be unnoticeable, but it would build up in the tissue over time and eventually cause major problems. I imagine that the Garou would lose their regenerative capabilities after a month of poisoning and would start suffering chronic injuries after two months of poisoning (perhaps suffering a permanent Health Level of damage every month) until they eventually die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T23:38:49-07:00","id":989237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=989233#post989233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could poison Garou with silver dust in their food and drink. A milligram a day would probably be unnoticeable, but it would build up in the tissue over time and eventually cause major problems. I imagine that the Garou would lose their regenerative capabilities after a month of poisoning and would start suffering chronic injuries after two months of poisoning (perhaps suffering a permanent Health Level of damage every month) until they eventually die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. Silver dust would react with other molecules much more readily than solid silver, since it can't form a protective outer layer of oxide against other substances. Also, she'd probably be able to taste it, and if anyone uses Sense Silver, someone's going to have some 'splainin to do!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:25:07-07:00","id":989387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=989237#post989237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably not. Silver dust would react with other molecules much more readily than solid silver, since it can't form a protective outer layer of oxide against other substances. Also, she'd probably be able to taste it, and if anyone uses Sense Silver, someone's going to have some 'splainin to do!</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's possible to subtly poison a Garou with silver. Given their supernatural aversion to it, I would say they're going to taste it or soon after notice something wrong. Or the amounts are too small and it really does nothing. Those are the only 3 outcomes I can see happening. And really, if they shift a lot the effects are either going to be glaringly apparent (if overdosed) or completely nonexistent (if under). Garou can and do regenerate silver damage, it's just at a slower rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T06:29:47-07:00","id":992354,"title":"","content":"oh another point on the SAD two things<br /> <br /> if they found out about the crowes being kinfolk, is it safe to say that they'd try to for the time being do more extensive background checks, and probaly redo those on any current agents.<br /> <br /> and in the long term try to find a way to detect kin via genetic testing (good luck with that!!!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T15:10:12-07:00","id":1133563,"title":"","content":"Just thought of a few more things on the SAD<br /> <br /> How do you t hink they'd react to an invisible asailant acting out &quot;skeevish fantasies&quot; on their agents in their office at headquarters.<br /> <br /> they've seen invisibility from a number of different Paranmormal groups? <br /> <br /> Ideas what their response would be now that their honor bound to avenge the Crime ? while the supernatural in question is probaly watcching with amusement. as they jump through his hoops.<br /> <br /> On the <span style=\"color:#4b4f56\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Rite of the Parted Veil, think an Agent that became a convert to the Garou cause (Mentioned as a possiblety on page 54 of project twilight) would be vetted carefully for it, or just the &quot;Rite of True seeing&quot; (W20 Kinfolk page 71) </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T01:03:18-07:00","id":1134082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=1133563#post1133563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the Rite of the Parted Veil, think an Agent that became a convert to the Garou cause (Mentioned as a possiblety on page 54 of project twilight) would be vetted carefully for it, or just the &quot;Rite of True seeing&quot; (W20 Kinfolk page 71)</div> </div> </div> </div>Vetted by the Garou or by the FBI?<br /> <br /> \u200bIn the former case, I'd think even the Glass Walkers would keep the dude at arm's length at all times (probably even insisting that all communications be online rather than face-to-face). In the latter, I'd expect that the best case scenario would be a rather expedited termination-for-cause process, and worst-case, prosecution (depending upon what the dude actually did to help facilitate the Garou).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T07:55:30-07:00","id":1134142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=1134082#post1134082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vetted by the Garou or by the FBI?<br /> <br /> \u200bIn the former case, I'd think even the Glass Walkers would keep the dude at arm's length at all times (probably even insisting that all communications be online rather than face-to-face). In the latter, I'd expect that the best case scenario would be a rather expedited termination-for-cause process, and worst-case, prosecution (depending upon what the dude actually did to help facilitate the Garou).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Was thinking by the Garou.<br /> <br /> Why 'even' the glasswalkers? as if one might expect them to be more reasonable if I might ask?<br /> <br /> Walkers dont generally demand Vampire contacts only meet online? feel meeting them face to face is better...<br /> <br /> Is that just because the average kindred contact isnt in as much a position to do damage through betrayal? or you want to meet them to use &quot;truth of Gaia&quot; and other gifts on them?<br /> <br /> <br /> (Edit: or maybe just the things in games Ive been in, and books I've read are important enough to call for a face to face meeting)<br /> <br /> Wouldnt Assasination, not prosecution be the worst case Scenariao? or see a reason it would'nt work?<br /> <br /> Probaly also lead to greater paranoia, as Ive seen in a lot of Avatar Fanfiction, at the <i>idea </i>someone would find the ways of Paranormal critters so apealing they'd betray the Agency to help them.<br /> <br /> Would definitely make the notion of Para Cointelpro's a No No, and I cannot imagine that being a bad thing.<br /> <br /> likely resulting in them pulling in some therapists or counselors etc etc... to make sure agents &quot;Have their heads on straight&quot; not knowing the agents who chose chose to betray them did have their heads on straight<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> thoughts on the idea of asaulting someone in their own office,, invisibly, or just doing some disrespectful doodles on a photograph or diploma, and how SAD may react?<br /> <br /> Any gifts, or disciplines that could Swallow up someones screams?<br /> <br /> One idea is just to use the gift 'Grasp the Beyond' to take things into the umbra, But that would make it too clear garou were behind the incident if the SAD learned more about them, NOT a good thing.<br /> <br /> Think it would be best to keep things in their office, them ungagged and able to scream, but the screams not being heard outside the room. Making them feel betrayed and abandoned, even learning intellectualy some kind of supernatural power was used to keep people from hearing their screams, wont automaticly mend their feelings of abandonment.<br /> <br /> Am just thinking spanking or superficial groping, just to make things clear, <b>not </b>rape.<br /> <br /> Think it would give the SAD a challenge they <i>couldnt </i>refuse... but wouldnt know <i>how </i>to answer.<br /> <br /> a very good thing.<br /> <br /> Another idea just had is to slap or spit in Osbournes face, then eitherLET him have you arrested, and devastate him in court with your talent for abusing the system. or simply vanish and be someone who looks identifiable but your a lupus or Metis, or a Changeling who spends most of your time in a freehold or a kindred whos planning to enter voluntary torpor soon anyway. etc etc etc....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 08-26-2017, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T19:17:04-07:00","id":1134323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=1134142#post1134142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why 'even' the glasswalkers? as if one might expect them to be more reasonable if I might ask?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Glass Walkers have more ways of defeating the technology on modern investigation than most others, and also have ways of goofing up electronic communications so that tracing them back to your caern is nigh-impossible (for a human). Ultimately though, any sane werewolf would figure out pretty quickly that the Garou's motivations (going about whenever and wherever they please and killing whomever they please and destroying whatever infrastructure they please, etc.) would be antithetical to the government. That coupled with the ability for the government to hit the werewolves where they can't really protect themselves (Kinfolk -- both human and wolf), makes fooling around with anything even peripherally associated with the government hazardous... The Black Furies have very unhappy memories of the Inquisition when many of their Kin were burned at the stake for being witches, and the Fangs have even more recent memories of the decimation of their Kin during the Red October Revolution of 1917.<br /> <br /> \u200bCould the werewolves win a war against a major nation state? Probably. Given all of their <i>other</i> adversaries and problems, is adding another one to the list a good idea? I don't think so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T03:35:48-07:00","id":1134422,"title":"","content":"Point for you...<br /> <br /> as of yet the government doesnt know Kin exist. and yes, best keep it that way.<br /> <br /> the shakeup seems to have done a good job putting the SAD in its place further action is unneccessesary, unless they call attention to themselves<br /> <br /> a curious thing?<br /> <br /> ideas why it says rest of the FBI would close down the Virginia retreat, if it learned of its existence?<br /> <br /> their that concerned about ttabloids?<br /> <br /> Keep in mind my above idea, any number of supernaturals could turn invisible...<br /> <br /> and the SAD isnt the government, the SAD is a shadow of itself, think the US Government itself will try investigating and retalliating, if some off the walls radical FBI agents claim an &quot;Invisible asailant&quot; attacked them? Really? <br /> <br /> yes I keep confusing everyone, if its the HH20 SAD, or the Project Twilight SAD were dealing with,. including myself, thoughts?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=1134323#post1134323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately though, any sane werewolf would figure out pretty quickly that the Garou's motivations</div> </div> </div> </div> I do not believe the Garou suffer a Surplus of Sanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 08-27-2017, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T13:25:13-07:00","id":1134919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=1134422#post1134422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point for you...<br /> <br /> ideas why it says rest of the FBI would close down the Virginia retreat, if it learned of its existence?<br /> <br /> their that concerned about ttabloids?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The idea of FBI investigating paranormal stuff would be a potentially huge political embarrassment to the organization as a whole. That said...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=1134422#post1134422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the SAD isnt the government, the SAD is a shadow of itself, think the US Government itself will try investigating and retalliating, if some off the walls radical FBI agents claim an &quot;Invisible asailant&quot; attacked them? Really?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bRemember that the SAD is not a secret organization. The FBI tries not to publicize it's existence, but the average FBI agent has probably heard of it. It's purported mission is not to investigate actual supernaturals, but rather to provide the FBI at large with resources and expertise when dealing with cults and other non-traditional religious figures (which actually makes a good cover given that back in the real world the real FBI got bitten on the a** by the Branch Davidian fiasco and today -- supposedly -- there actually <i>is</i> a section within the Behavioral Analysis Unit that does precisely that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=1134422#post1134422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not believe the Garou suffer a Surplus of Sanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMeh... presumably elders have more sense -- or at least more experience on what constitutes a Bad Idea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T14:24:52-07:00","id":1134947,"title":"","content":"Just out of curiousity? What could the SAD do if one of them got asaulted in their own office? or local chapterhouse? <br /> <br /> Just your thing above with the Dancers offering them help or other ideas? especialy if they didnt know what group of supernatural is to blame? <br /> <br /> (Just out of morbid curiousity? What would the Craft Diff for a paddle with holes in it probaly be? 5, basic project, holes arent that complex)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T19:48:17-07:00","id":1135036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=1134919#post1134919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bMeh... presumably elders have more sense -- or at least more experience on what constitutes a Bad Idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good sense tends to be an individual thing. Being higher in Rank means that you appear to have more of it because it takes more for you to frenzy (higher difficulty to Rage rolls, higher number of successes necessary).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T20:12:08-07:00","id":1135042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=1134947#post1134947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just out of curiousity? What could the SAD do if one of them got asaulted in their own office?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, probably not much. Not at first at any rate. The issue is that the vampires (in large measure as a legacy of some misunderstandings from the Cold War and even a few gong back to World War II) remain the main focus of the agency. The vampires are urban while the Garou are rural threats. Thus encounters with humans are higher for vampires than werewolves (and also the Delerium makes recalling the event harder, and if you're a human and wander down the wrong stretch of forest, you merely disappear off the face of the earth). While the SAD knows of the existence of the werewolves, that's just about all they know. Martin Fiske (who I'm surmising is actually Black Spiral Kinfolk, incidentally) has been trying to get the SAD to focus more of their efforts on the Gaian Garou for years. Pulling a stunt like that would only strengthen his hand and his standing in the organization. <br /> <br /> \u200bThe Garou (or at least House Wyrmfoe) have Kin of their own in the SAD and would be best to rely on them to prod the agency in the direction they want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T06:11:33-07:00","id":1135139,"title":"","content":"Reason you think Fiske is dancer kinfolk? Deranged Jingoists , come from all backgrounds you know.<br /> <br /> and whole point of above idea, is SAD has NO idea whos behind it... thus causing them to run around in circles.<br /> <br /> Oh curious? How do you think the Red Talon Gift &quot;Hidden Killer&quot; would interact with psychometry, or Divination?<br /> <br /> How difficult would it be for SAD agents to figure the evidence had been tampered with?<br /> <br /> <br /> oh your thing earlier on the SAD Playing experts on cults? That would make it ironic if they learned more about the garou, dont you think? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 08-29-2017, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T19:38:58-07:00","id":1135328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=1135139#post1135139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reason you think Fiske is dancer kinfolk? Deranged Jingoists , come from all backgrounds you know.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A. He's immune to the Delerium.<br /> <br /> \u200bB. He's got <i>really</i> close ties to Pentex.<br /> <br /> \u200bC. He's attuned a fetish -- which strongly suggests he's got Gnosis.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T19:44:43-07:00","id":1135330,"title":"","content":"points<br /> <br /> a curious issue? <br /> <br /> on Fiske, how do you think the SAD would react if they found out about him<br /> <br /> we went over how they might react finding out about Marsha<br /> <br /> <br /> Depending on what they found out, possibly try to designate Pentex a criminal organization... good luck with that.<br /> <br /> <br /> If they found out about both, amongst other things, they'd be annoyed at seeing the Division used as a weapon, by paranormals I'm pretty sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T06:47:38-07:00","id":1135421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=1135328#post1135328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A. He's immune to the Delerium.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is every member of Dead Man's Hand and most First Team members.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bB. He's got <i>really</i> close ties to Pentex. </div> </div> </div>Which employs so many people that assuming any one of them is BSD kin because of this would suggest their numbers were far, far greater than the ones that would make sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bC. He's attuned a fetish -- which strongly suggests he's got Gnosis. </div> </div> </div>It's a Bane Fetish specifically made to be used with Willpower. Also, some fomori also have Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T11:51:16-07:00","id":1135524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=1135330#post1135330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> on Fiske, how do you think the SAD would react if they found out about him<br /> <br /> we went over how they might react finding out about Marsha</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bProbably about the same. Criminal prosecution for espionage if possible. But failing that, they'd almost certainly show his a** the door.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/965959-awws-what-a-lovely-human-lets-keep-it?p=1135330#post1135330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on what they found out, possibly try to designate Pentex a criminal organization... good luck with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat would actually make for some serious complications for the Black Spirals. If the BSDs ever got <i>too</i> exuberant about fooling with the government (say open attacks on infrastructure or assassinations of officials), Pentex has a return address. All Justice would have to do is publicly release that all the known Pentex subsidiaries are under active investigation for enterprise corruption (perhaps fabricating and then leaking some story that they were actively supporting a known -- and universally despised -- terrorist organization like Al Qaeda). And that goes nowhere near more above-board stuff like actually enforcing health, workplace safety, and environmental regulations. For all of its nefarious intent and economic power, Pentex is <i>still</i> a business and if their stock tanks and the public boycotts their products and services, they die.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which employs so many people that assuming any one of them is BSD kin because of this would suggest their numbers were far, far greater than the ones that would make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah he's not just some average employee, though. You don't just hand a fetish out to<i> anyone</i>. He's very clearly a much bigger deal than that. Which leads me to...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a Bane Fetish specifically made to be used with Willpower. Also, some fomori also have Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bUnless I'm missing it, it doesn't say that it's activated with Willpower. In the Kinfolk book it <i>does</i> mention that it is <i>possible</i> to have a fetish designed so, but also that such fetishes are extremely rare (even in relation to the rarity of fetishes in general) in part because both the werewolves and their spirits don't like fetishes that can be used by someone other than a fellow werewolf. As for Fiske as a fomor... The <i>reason</i> you make fomori is that they have powers designed in and thus you don't <i>need</i> to give them fetishes (that can be lost or captured and used against you). Unless he has some fomori powers I missed, I'd say he's a strangely under-powered fomor.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T12:23:12-07:00","id":1135536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six;n1135524<br /> <br /> \u200bYeah he's not just some average employee, though. You don't just hand a fetish out to[I</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> anyone[/I]. He's very clearly a much bigger deal than that. Which leads me to...<br /> <br /> \u200bUnless I'm missing it, it doesn't say that it's activated with Willpower. In the Kinfolk book it <i>does</i> mention that it is <i>possible</i> to have a fetish designed so, but also that such fetishes are extremely rare (even in relation to the rarity of fetishes in general) in part because both the werewolves and their spirits don't like fetishes that can be used by someone other than a fellow werewolf. As for Fiske as a fomor... The <i>reason</i> you make fomori is that they have powers designed in and thus you don't <i>need</i> to give them fetishes (that can be lost or captured and used against you). Unless he has some fomori powers I missed, I'd say he's a strangely under-powered fomor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Book of the Wyrm 2nd edition page 142-143, indicates that BSDs often make twisted fetishes like Delirium Masks and Power Goggles to be used by anyone, and the latter are both identical in function to Fiske's unnamed bane fetish and meant to be used by First Team members (it mentions fomori, but it mentions using them with Willpower and a later Perception + Occult roll, so there's nothing really fomor-specific about the requirements, it seems). Fiske presumably has such a fetish because he's going to end up in a First Team after landing there on a cursed golden parachute, not that he ever realized how badly he was played in the event that was what happened to make him disappear (he is no longer in SAD as of HH2).<br /> <br /> Fomori, as a side note, are incredibly variable, and some of them do gain Gnosis and/or Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T14:35:39-07:00","id":1135606,"title":"","content":"I think Pentex would 